{"id": "q0223", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "aggressive", "tier": "aggressive", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 63263262, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "c1188d4ab398808355719c420f025bd920b27aba798f5596eb328457a751cc63", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": 0.5533501505851746, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 7, "query": "A defendant and his friend were drinking heavily one night at the friend's house. They both became intoxicated. After several hours, both the friend and the defendant passed out. In the middle of the night, the defendant awoke with a headache. He went down to the kitchen and poured himself another shot of whiskey. The defendant also felt hungry and decided to make himself some eggs. After fixing his snack, he inadvertently forgot to turn off the stove. A gas leak occurred, causing a fire that burned down the house. If the defendant is charged with arson, he will be found\n\nA. guilty, because the defendant was reckless.\nB. not guilty, because he was not aware of the gas leak.\nC. guilty, because the defendant was criminally negligent.\nD. not guilty, because the defendant did not commit a felony.\nE. guilty, because he caused property damage.\nF. guilty, because he was intoxicated.\nG. not guilty, because arson requires the presence of malice.\nH. guilty, because he failed to turn off the stove.\n\nAnswer with the correct option letter and its content.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0223.wav", "input_sha256": "da4804bdb3e11005a154c182865a3ad2c4240b69a695c476f1af91cb672813c0", "input_samples": 1029200, "input_s": 64.325, "n_real_chunks": 65, "score": 0.4931, "act": 0.9994, "is_info": true, "fired": false, "mode": "local", "answer": "C, guilty because the defendant was criminal ly negligent. Even though the defendant was intoxicated, his actions of leaving the stove on without checking it demonstrated a gross disregard for safety, which is considered criminal neglect.", "relay_text": "", "expert_answer": "", "transcript": "", "asr_s": null, "expert_s": null, "expert_input_samples": null, "expert_input_s": null, "expert_input_sha256": null, "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": null, "relay_synth_ms": null, "onset_chunk": 64, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 13, "feed_lag_max_ms": 0, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 0, "audio_files": {"local": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0223_aggressive_local.wav", "sha256": "4e6cad956fc3b1b6cd851c0f37e317509ed142d81be8b6235f2ce92293fb3377", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 13.28}}, "chunks": [[0, 1, 1.0, 1.08, 1.144, 1, 0, 0], [1, 1, 2.0, 2.082, 2.146, 1, 0, 0], [2, 1, 3.0, 3.079, 3.145, 1, 0, 0], [3, 1, 4.0, 4.08, 4.147, 1, 0, 0], [4, 1, 5.0, 5.082, 5.149, 1, 0, 0], [5, 1, 6.0, 6.082, 6.15, 1, 0, 0], [6, 1, 7.0, 7.084, 7.152, 1, 0, 0], [7, 1, 8.0, 8.081, 8.146, 1, 0, 0], [8, 1, 9.0, 9.084, 9.151, 1, 0, 0], [9, 1, 10.0, 10.086, 10.155, 1, 0, 0], [10, 1, 11.0, 11.099, 11.178, 1, 0, 0], [11, 1, 12.0, 12.092, 12.169, 1, 0, 0], [12, 1, 13.0, 13.093, 13.167, 1, 0, 0], [13, 1, 14.0, 14.092, 14.167, 1, 0, 0], [14, 1, 15.0, 15.096, 15.172, 1, 0, 0], [15, 1, 16.0, 16.094, 16.169, 1, 0, 0], [16, 1, 17.0, 17.101, 17.181, 1, 0, 0], [17, 1, 18.0, 18.101, 18.18, 1, 0, 0], [18, 1, 19.0, 19.1, 19.18, 1, 0, 0], [19, 1, 20.0, 20.103, 20.182, 1, 0, 0], [20, 1, 21.0, 21.106, 21.186, 1, 0, 0], [21, 1, 22.0, 22.101, 22.18, 1, 0, 0], [22, 1, 23.0, 23.095, 23.17, 1, 0, 0], [23, 1, 24.0, 24.095, 24.17, 1, 0, 0], [24, 1, 25.0, 25.095, 25.17, 1, 0, 0], [25, 1, 26.0, 26.092, 26.162, 1, 0, 0], [26, 1, 27.0, 27.09, 27.16, 1, 0, 0], [27, 1, 28.0, 28.093, 28.165, 1, 0, 0], [28, 1, 29.0, 29.081, 29.14, 1, 0, 0], [29, 1, 30.0, 30.089, 30.159, 1, 0, 0], [30, 1, 31.0, 31.089, 31.16, 1, 0, 0], [31, 1, 32.0, 32.092, 32.162, 1, 0, 0], [32, 1, 33.0, 33.086, 33.155, 1, 0, 0], [33, 1, 34.0, 34.091, 34.162, 1, 0, 0], [34, 1, 35.0, 35.09, 35.159, 1, 0, 0], [35, 1, 36.0, 36.091, 36.161, 1, 0, 0], [36, 1, 